<!--
  The catalog's user-visible copy, as Compose Multiplatform string resources.

  Every string a sticker RENDERS lives here, so a render carrying `localeTag` (or a
  `@Preview(locale = …)`) resolves it translated. What deliberately stays a Kotlin literal:
  design-system token names (`primary`, `Display Large`, `XS`), which are API identifiers rather
  than copy; sample data that is not language (`10:30`, `alice@example.com`, `⌘E`, the person
  names); and the annotation metadata (ids, captions), which is catalog chrome the renderer never
  paints into a sticker.
-->
